{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/827856-book-with-kingdom-descriptions","id":827856,"title":"Book with Kingdom Descriptions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-10T16:46:18-08:00","id":827856,"title":"Book with Kingdom Descriptions?","content":"I remember there being a book that dealt with the Kingdom of Willows (Southeast US) but I couldn't remember if there was any book or books that had information on the various other kingdoms in the US or internationally. I don't remember there being a Rage Across the World type book for Changeling but I could be wrong. Does anyone know where I can find more info on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T23:35:10-08:00","id":828038,"title":"","content":"There's no global overview along the lines of Rage Across the World. However, Fool's Luck has a page taking a brief look at Kithain around the world.<br /> <br /> There're no other books on the North American kingdoms proper.<br /> <br /> Shadows on the Hill covers Hawai'i, which is considered part of the Kingdom of Pacifica, Court of All Kings covers Ireland, and Isle of the Mighty covers Britain.<br /> <br /> Land of Eight Million Dreams gives an overview of the hsien, and how they've organised East Asia.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness: Blood-Dimmed Tides takes us beneath the waves to the courts of the merfolk.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T05:05:04-08:00","id":828148,"title":"","content":"Nobles: The Shinning Host takes a brief look at Kithain around the US (Concordia). Pages 51-53.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:24:40-08:00","id":828387,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses. I will check out the ones on Ireland and Britain for sure. Here's hoping we get a bit more info in the 20th Anniversary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T15:24:23-08:00","id":828468,"title":"","content":"Isle of the Mighty (Britain) is so wrong... It's a fun read, but it's obviously written by non-Brits. For example, my home city of Manchester is described as being in the Midlands, when anyone in England would call it the North. In the UK, the North refers to the North of England, not the North of the UK, so it's basically anything above the Watford Gap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 02-12-2016, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T16:56:25-08:00","id":828498,"title":"","content":"That's funny because I've been reading the Changeling books after the Kickstarter and Court of All Kings is actually extremely good/accurate. My eyes nearly fell out of my head at parts since the writer showed genuine knowledge of certain things (e.g. the Gaelic spelling reform) most Irish people aren't even aware of.<br /> <br /> Also some of its art is beyond beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T07:55:04-08:00","id":828786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/